\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {1}{\ignorespaces What the comparison contains decides the answer. Distances are normalised by the typical nearest-neighbour separation of the space in hand, and a valid match requires a normalised distance below the dashed threshold \emph  {and} a distance smaller than that to every compound not designated a simulant. (a) Thirty-five-compound panel, merged space: nearest incumbent simulant (circles) and nearest candidate once the five literature-used compounds are admitted (diamonds). (b) Matched agents over 1000 descriptor-resampling replicates; circles means, rules medians, bars the 2.5th to 97.5th percentiles. (c) Twenty-eight-compound panel, the three spaces; filled markers are valid matches. (d) Exact permutation null for that panel over all 680 designations, actual designation marked, mean-difference statistic (Benjamini-Hochberg over the eighteen tests, 0.163). (e) Volatility axis, in $\log _{10}(P/\mathrm  {mmHg})$; the one pairing inside the criterion, soman to DPGME, lies 0.0107 decades apart. Section~\ref {res:panels} and Supporting Information Sections~\ref {S-meth:dboot} and~\ref {S-meth:vol} give the constructions.}}{12}{}\protected@file@percent }
